expression","windows":{"definition":[["A statement made from inputs and the operators AND, OR and NOT that evaluates to ",{"answer":"True or False"}," (1 or 0)."]],"characteristics":[["Written in the form Q = (A AND B) OR C. The same logic can be shown as a logic diagram or a ",{"answer":"truth table"},". Work out any brackets first."]],"examples":[["Half-price if student (A) or has a card (B), but not on Saturday (C): Q = (A OR B) AND ",{"answer":"NOT C"},"."]],"nonExamples":[["total = a + b is arithmetic, not Boolean, because it gives a number. A Boolean expression only ever evaluates to one of ",{"answer":"two"}," values: 1 or 0."]]},"wordBank":["NOT C","True or False","truth table","two"],"sketch":{"cloze":{"page":8,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688},"answers":{"page":9,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688}}},{"term":"Combining logic gates","windows":{"definition":[["Connecting gates so that the ",{"answer":"output"}," of one gate becomes an input of the next, to model a problem with several conditions."]],"characteristics":[["Each gate matches one ",{"answer":"operator"}," in the expression. The bracketed part is drawn first, nearest the inputs. The final gate gives the output Q."]],"examples":[["Aged 15 or over (A) and has a ticket (B) or money (C): Q = A AND (B OR C). The ",{"answer":"brackets"}," put OR first."]],"nonExamples":[["NOT A AND NOT B cannot be drawn as one gate. It needs two NOT gates feeding an AND gate, so ",{"answer":"three gates"}," in total."]]},"wordBank":["brackets","operator","output","three gates"],"sketch":{"cloze":{"page":11,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688},"answers":{"page":12,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688}}},{"term":"Truth table for a logic circuit","windows":{"definition":[["A table showing the output of a whole logic circuit for ",{"answer":"every combination"}," of its inputs."]],"characteristics":[["Add a column for each ",{"answer"