"},", so users need both the source code and the interpreter. Interpreted programs run more slowly."]]},"wordBank":["debugging","error","executable file","one line at a time"],"sketch":{"cloze":{"page":8,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688},"answers":{"page":9,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688}}},{"term":"High-level language","windows":{"definition":[["A programming language that uses ",{"answer":"English-like"}," keywords, so it is easy for humans to read and write, such as Python."]],"characteristics":[["Portable: the same code can run on different computers. One statement becomes many machine code instructions. Must be ",{"answer":"translated"}," before it can run."]],"examples":[["The same Python program, e.g. print(\\"Hi\\"), can run on a laptop or a phone with a different ",{"answer":"processor"},"."]],"nonExamples":[["High-level does not mean the CPU understands it. The CPU only executes ",{"answer":"machine code"},", so a compiler or an interpreter is always needed."]]},"wordBank":["English-like","machine code","processor","translated"],"sketch":{"cloze":{"page":11,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688},"answers":{"page":12,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688}}},{"term":"Low-level language","windows":{"definition":[["A language that is close to the hardware, machine code or assembly language, written for one specific type of ",{"answer":"processor"},"."]],"characteristics":[["Gives direct control of ",{"answer":"memory"}," and hardware. Programs can run faster and take up less space, but are harder to write, read and debug."]],"examples":[["Code for ",{"answer":"embedded systems"},", e.g. a microwave controller, may be low-level to control the hardware directly."]],"nonExamples":[["A short Python program is not low-level. Level means how close the code is to machine code, not its length or difficulty. Low-level code is not ",{"answer":"portable"},"."]]},"wordBank":["embedded systems","memory","portable","processor"],"sketch":{"cloze":{"page":14,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688},"answers":{"page":15,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688}}},{"term":"Translator","windows":{"definition":[["Software that converts program code written in one language into ",{"answer":"machine code"}," so that the processor can execute it."]],"characteristics":[["J277 covers two translators for high-level code: the compiler and the interpreter. Without one, the ",{"answer":"processor"}," could not run a high-level program."]],"examples":[["A compiler produces an executable file; an interpreter produces ",{"answer":"no"}," executable and translates on every run."]],"nonExamples":[["An editor lets you write code but does not translate it. Machine code needs ",{"answer":"no translation"},": it already runs directly on the processor."]]},"wordBank":["machine code","no","no translation","processor"],"sketch":{"cloze":{"page":17,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688},"answers":{"page":18,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688}}},{"term":"Machine code","windows":{"definition":[["Program instructions written in ",{"answer":"binary"}," that the processor can execute directly, without any translation."]],"characteristics":[["The lowest-level language. It is ",{"answer":"processor specific"},", and very hard for humans to read or debug."]],"examples":[["10110000 01100001 is one machine code instruction; a compiled ",{"answer":"executable"}," file is full of them."]],"nonExamples":[["Assembly such as ADD 5, or Python, is not machine code. Both must be ",{"answer":"translated"}," before the processor can run them."]]},"wordBank":["binary","executable","processor specific","translated"],"sketch":{"cloze":{"page":20,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688},"answers":{"page":21,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688}}},{"term":"Source code","windows":{"definition":[["The program code written by the programmer in a ",{"answer":"high-level language"},", before it is translated."]],"characteristics":[["Humans can read and edit it. It must be ",{"answer":"translated"}," before it can run. Compiled software is shared without it, so users cannot copy or modify the code."]],"examples":[["A saved file holding lines such as score = score + 1, typed into the IDE's ",{"answer":"editor"},", is source code."]],"nonExamples":[["The executable file made by a compiler is not source code: it is ",{"answer":"machine code"},". End users of compiled software never see the source code."]]},"wordBank":["editor","high-level language","machine code","translated"],"sketch":{"cloze":{"page":23,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688},"answers":{"page":24,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688}}},{"term":"Assembly language","windows":{"definition":[["A low-level language that uses short ",{"answer":"mnemonics"},", such as ADD and SUB, in place of binary machine code instructions."]],"characteristics":[["One assembly instruction represents ",{"answer":"one"}," machine code instruction. It is processor specific and gives direct control of hardware, but is easier to read than binary."]],"examples":[["LDA 5, ADD 6, STO 7: load a value, add another to it, then store the result back in ",{"answer":"memory"},"."]],"nonExamples":[["Assembly is not high-level just because it uses words. It is not portable, and it must still be ",{"answer":"translated"}," into machine code before it can run."]]},"wordBank":["memory","mnemonics","one","translated"],"sketch":{"cloze":{"page":26,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688},"answers":{"page":27,"top":0.3297,"bottom":0.6507,"left":0.7308,"right":0.9688}}}]},{"source":"data/pdf/j277/module-resources/2.5/frayer-2.pdf","sourceSha256":"a4c3c5effd7ece5f7f27d4be7601deae338f91000192f250bab584c8ccbce32c","code":"2.5.2","title":"Integrated Development Environments